 The Dev lifecycle is the core delivery workflow. Every ticket — feature, bug fix, chore — runs through it. Its job is to ensure that code is planned against the architecture, implemented step-by-step with verification, tested before merge, and documented before close.
 
+Two operational stages run ahead of Plan: **Context Gathering** captures the ticket's
+intent once (tracker/Confluence/approved design/developer input) as `intent.md`, and
+**Ceremony** is the official start of work (tracker transition + branch checkout).
+They exist so Plan can stay dedicated to planning only. The major blocks below —
+Plan, Implement, Test, Document — are unchanged by this; see Phases for the full
+six-stage breakdown.
+
